WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.757
Module 3: building it in SurveyCraft.

00:00:02.757 --> 00:00:05.886
You've designed the huddle pulse on paper.

00:00:05.886 --> 00:00:11.101
Now you'll build it: questions,
blocks, logic, messages and languages.

00:00:11.101 --> 00:00:12.591
About forty minutes.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:16.094
Click New Survey at the top of any page.

00:00:16.094 --> 00:00:18.414
Most people start from scratch.

00:00:18.414 --> 00:00:24.625
If the client already has the survey in
Qualtrics, you can import its file instead.

00:00:24.625 --> 00:00:30.463
Give the survey a clear name, file it in
a project if you like, and create it.

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:34.279
It opens in the builder
with one block, in English.

00:00:34.279 --> 00:00:40.192
One warning about imports: questions and
blocks come across, but logic doesn't.

00:00:40.192 --> 00:00:41.913
Rebuild it and test it.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:44.416
The builder has four parts.

00:00:44.416 --> 00:00:50.092
On the left, the question types: click
one to add it, or drag it into place.

00:00:50.092 --> 00:00:52.556
Next to that, the blocks outline.

00:00:52.556 --> 00:00:57.559
In the middle, the canvas, where
your questions sit block by block.

00:00:57.559 --> 00:01:03.234
And on the right, question properties,
which open when you click a question.

00:01:03.234 --> 00:01:08.760
SurveyCraft saves automatically a couple
of seconds after you stop typing.

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:14.212
The toolbar has undo and redo, test
responses, add from library, preview,

00:01:14.212 --> 00:01:17.273
request assistance, and Next: Distribute.

00:01:17.767 --> 00:01:20.738
The question types come in five groups.

00:01:20.738 --> 00:01:26.606
Basic: multiple choice, checkboxes,
short and long text, dropdowns and dates.

00:01:26.606 --> 00:01:31.864
Rating and scales: sliders, Net
Promoter Score and the Likert matrix.

00:01:31.864 --> 00:01:37.426
Advanced: ranking, constant sum, side
by side, heat maps and drill-downs.

00:01:37.426 --> 00:01:42.379
Content: file uploads, and text
or image blocks for instructions.

00:01:42.379 --> 00:01:48.399
And the narrative group, which powers
Mosaic Signal and is taught in the Mosaic

00:01:48.399 --> 00:01:52.590
Signal course of the Mosaic
Practitioner certification.

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:55.409
Most pulses need only a few of these.

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:58.568
A few properties do most of the work.

00:01:58.568 --> 00:02:02.463
Required, for the questions
you can't analyse without,

00:02:02.463 --> 00:02:05.203
like department or a routing question.

00:02:05.203 --> 00:02:08.305
Keep sensitive and open
questions optional.

00:02:08.305 --> 00:02:10.540
"Other" adds a write-in option.

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:15.156
Randomize options shuffles an
unordered list, but never a scale.

00:02:15.156 --> 00:02:19.483
Reverse scored flips a negatively
worded item in the export.

00:02:19.483 --> 00:02:20.276
And piping.

00:02:20.276 --> 00:02:23.378
Give a question a short
alias, like "dept",

00:02:23.378 --> 00:02:27.128
then write it in curly
brackets in a later question,

00:02:27.128 --> 00:02:29.868
and each person sees their own answer.

00:02:29.868 --> 00:02:34.196
Add a fallback, like "your team",
for anyone who skipped it.

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:36.018
Blocks are sections.

00:02:36.018 --> 00:02:39.181
Use them to group questions,
move them together,

00:02:39.181 --> 00:02:41.883
and give skip logic somewhere to jump to.

00:02:41.883 --> 00:02:44.651
You can also show a block only to leaders.

00:02:44.651 --> 00:02:50.120
In Settings, under Leader Configuration,
pick the question that identifies leaders,

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:53.481
like a role question, and
tick which answers count.

00:02:53.481 --> 00:02:55.985
Put that question in an earlier block.

00:02:55.985 --> 00:02:58.094
Then mark the block leader-only.

00:02:58.094 --> 00:02:59.412
Nobody else sees it.

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:01.748
Logic lives on its own tab.

00:03:01.748 --> 00:03:05.649
Pick a question, then choose
display logic or skip logic.

00:03:05.649 --> 00:03:11.123
Display logic sits on the question that
might be hidden: show this question when

00:03:11.123 --> 00:03:12.971
certain answers were given.

00:03:12.971 --> 00:03:18.446
Skip logic sits on the question people
answer before jumping: when this happens,

00:03:18.446 --> 00:03:22.689
skip to another question, another
block, the end of the block,

00:03:22.689 --> 00:03:24.400
or the end of the survey.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:28.574
Skip rules run in order, and
the first one that matches wins.

00:03:28.574 --> 00:03:33.775
And don't worry about required questions
that someone never saw; SurveyCraft

00:03:33.775 --> 00:03:35.897
doesn't hold them up for those.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:38.288
Here's the huddle branch.

00:03:38.288 --> 00:03:44.330
The routing question asks whether people
took part in a cross-site huddle in the

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:45.160
last month.

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:51.353
On the two follow-ups about whether huddles
help and whether problems get followed

00:03:51.353 --> 00:03:55.506
up, add display logic: show
when the answer equals yes.

00:03:55.506 --> 00:03:59.207
On the barriers question,
show when it equals no.

00:03:59.207 --> 00:04:00.566
Then open Preview.

00:04:00.566 --> 00:04:04.720
Answer yes, and you should
see the two follow-ups only.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:09.704
Go back, answer no, and you should
see the barriers question only.

00:04:09.704 --> 00:04:12.423
You'll test it at scale in Module 4.

00:04:12.933 --> 00:04:14.394
Four traps to avoid.

00:04:14.394 --> 00:04:18.118
SurveyCraft lets a condition
point at any question,

00:04:18.118 --> 00:04:20.967
even one the person hasn't reached yet,

00:04:20.967 --> 00:04:24.399
so base every condition
on an earlier question.

00:04:24.399 --> 00:04:26.590
Put specific skip rules first.

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:31.848
If you rename or delete an answer
option, check every rule that used it.

00:04:31.848 --> 00:04:33.309
And test every path.

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:36.155
In Settings, write your messages.

00:04:36.155 --> 00:04:41.651
The welcome message carries your promise:
purpose, time, that it's voluntary,

00:04:41.651 --> 00:04:45.362
what's confidential, and
when people will hear back.

00:04:45.362 --> 00:04:48.573
The thank-you message
says what happens next.

00:04:48.573 --> 00:04:53.641
The closed message greets anyone who
opens the link after you close it.

00:04:53.641 --> 00:04:59.493
Respondents also see a short privacy line
and a private link that lets them delete

00:04:59.493 --> 00:05:00.706
their own answer.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:07.012
To offer more languages, set your primary
language, add the ones you need, save,

00:05:07.012 --> 00:05:08.029
and translate.

00:05:08.029 --> 00:05:12.533
An AI translator fills in the
questions, options and messages.

00:05:12.533 --> 00:05:17.764
Then have a fluent speaker check every
one, especially the scale labels.

00:05:17.764 --> 00:05:19.144
Two things to know.

00:05:19.144 --> 00:05:24.811
The first time you publish, SurveyCraft
translates into every offered language

00:05:24.811 --> 00:05:29.025
before the survey goes live,
which can take a few minutes,

00:05:29.025 --> 00:05:31.059
so only offer what you need.

00:05:31.059 --> 00:05:35.418
And the survey's text goes to
an AI service for translation.

00:05:35.418 --> 00:05:37.380
Respondents' answers don't.

00:05:37.867 --> 00:05:41.900
Themes hold the colours, font
and logo respondents see.

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:47.401
On a survey's Theme tab, pick a theme
or make one, upload a logo, and save.

00:05:47.401 --> 00:05:49.968
Then check how it looks in Preview.

00:05:49.968 --> 00:05:55.395
The Question Library is a searchable
bank of questions for your workspace.

00:05:55.395 --> 00:06:00.089
In the builder, choose Save to
library on a question to keep it,

00:06:00.089 --> 00:06:02.583
and Add from library to reuse one.

00:06:02.583 --> 00:06:04.930
Instrument items stay out of it.

00:06:05.433 --> 00:06:07.471
Quick check before Module 4.

00:06:07.967 --> 00:06:08.784
To sum up.

00:06:08.784 --> 00:06:11.236
Rebuild logic after an import.

00:06:11.236 --> 00:06:16.876
Use the simplest question types,
and Required only where you need it.

00:06:16.876 --> 00:06:22.271
Display logic shows a question;
skip logic sends people elsewhere.

00:06:22.271 --> 00:06:23.579
Test every path.

00:06:23.579 --> 00:06:26.358
And get every translation checked.

00:06:26.358 --> 00:06:30.119
Next, Module 4: settings,
privacy and testing.

